WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.680
We have a voicemail number, which you can
call anytime.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.030
The numbers, two one nine two.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:14.549
David P. here is just an absolutely delightful
caller saying my metaphore about crawling

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:17.630
over broken glass to vote for Biden.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.560
She says it literally applies to her.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.670
Take a listen to this.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.670
Hi, David.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.869
This is your father in law, Florida, who can
only get you on Facebook, too.

00:00:26.869 --> 00:00:31.509
I just wanted to tell you that when you said
some people would crawl over broken glass

00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:32.509
to vote.

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:35.620
I burst out laughing because it was funny.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.310
But because you were describing me to a T..

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.820
I already voted by mail in my primary.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:41.820
Good.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.520
I'm 68 years old and I've been stressing for
four years.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.950
So I'm likely to die from the virus.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:53.390
But now I intend to wear a double mask and
turn in my ballot to vote in person.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:56.820
Nothing will stop me from voting against Trump.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:00.140
I just hope, beyond hope, there are enough
of us.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.040
Keep up the great work, David.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.670
What a caller.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:05.670
What a caller.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.090
Just absolutely fantastic.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:12.050
And, you know, there's debates over who's
motivated, which party is more motivated or

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.150
less motivated or what.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:21.400
It's going to come down to individuals like
our terrific caller who say I'm going to figure

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:28.890
out how to vote and whether I'm figuratively
crawling over broken glass, which includes

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:32.570
crawling, getting around the landmines of
voter suppression that are being placed out

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:40.600
there or literally crawling over broken glass
or what may be, you know, understaffed and

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:46.680
under-resourced polling places or whatever
the case may be, wearing two masks, etc. up.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.200
She's going to figure out how to vote.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.440
And that's ultimately what this election is
going to come down to.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.850
We have a fantastic bonus show for you today.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:59.960
There is a call from pediatricians to end
these active shooter trainings that have become

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.830
very common in schools.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:06.910
And their argument is that the trainings do
relatively little if there is actually an

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:08.000
active shooter.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.799
It's such a chaotic situation that the trainings
really don't do much.

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:14.300
But the fact that the trainings are happening
may be traumatizing to students and may be

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:18.620
causing them to live in what is still statistically
an irrational fear given the low likelihood

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.120
of an active shooter scenario.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.079
I want to talk about that.

00:02:22.079 --> 00:02:27.489
